dialogue greenvalley_party_talk
title: A lantern that should be dead
trigger: ThemeStart greenvalley
when: NpcJoined merchant
speaker commander $commander
speaker trusted $trusted
speaker merchant - name='Lantern Merchant' portrait=courier

node a commander
  The Tithe Moors. Every hold has paid, and the white wagons still come. I don't know these hills. I don't know why I'm walking them.
  -> b

node b merchant
  Three times the quota this year, and nobody says why. And that lantern on the caravan had been dead longer than my grandmother. It lit in your hand. So when you remember who you are, I'd like to hear it.
  * You've been quiet by the wagon. Say what you're thinking. -> speak
    if: TrustAtLeast $trusted 25
  * When I remember, you'll be the first to hear it.

node speak trusted
  Everyone I know paid the tithe, and none of us asked where it went. You don't even know your own name, and you're already asking. I'd sooner follow that than wait for the next wagon.
  * Then walk beside me, not behind. I'll need someone who knows these hills. -> beside
    do: AddTrust $trusted 6
  * Keep asking with me. Two people asking are harder to ignore. -> asking
    do: AddTrust $trusted 3

node beside trusted
  Beside, then. I know which holds will feed us and which will sell us. That's a start.

node asking trusted
  Harder to ignore. And harder to tithe white, maybe.
